WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.860
- While Maria was filming this movie,

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:03.860
she got some news about
a certain nomination

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:05.160
for her role in Borat.

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:08.053
And Judd actually got it on
camera, so let's see that.

00:00:09.478 --> 00:00:12.228
(knocks on door)

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:16.972
- Where's Ron Junn?

00:00:16.972 --> 00:00:17.805
- Action.

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:20.720
- Where's Ron Junn?

00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:30.475
- You were just nominated
for an Academy Award, man.

00:00:30.475 --> 00:00:32.305
- Ah! (beep). Oh my God! (laughing)

00:00:32.305 --> 00:00:35.972
(everyone claps and cheers)

00:00:38.974 --> 00:00:41.974
(audience clapping)

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:45.640
- You're so kinda to capture it.

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:47.719
I love that! You were, first of all,

00:00:47.719 --> 00:00:50.260
why are you so scared at first?

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:51.093
- Because

00:00:51.093 --> 00:00:51.926
(female guest laughs)

00:00:51.926 --> 00:00:53.187
- Does he beat you on set?

00:00:53.187 --> 00:00:56.563
- No! So here's the thing,
usually when we've been working,

00:00:56.563 --> 00:00:58.490
Judd is gonna be incredible
and he's gonna say

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:01.520
on the mic some lines to
improvise and think about it.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:02.640
And everybody can hear him,

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:04.004
but this time it was like action.

00:01:04.004 --> 00:01:05.560
And I see that somebody's coming,

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:09.280
I'm like, oh holy (beep). It's
that bad that he is not...

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:10.113
- He has to walk over?

00:01:10.113 --> 00:01:11.980
- ...comfortable to say it
out loud, people to hear it.

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:13.910
I'm like, how terrible. That was the scene

00:01:13.910 --> 00:01:16.380
when we supposed to like
touch hands and hand

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:19.730
over hand, and my hands
are like shaking crazily

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:22.180
because I can see that
it's 12-oh-something,

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:24.150
it's time when the thing is happening.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:26.367
He's coming closer, I'm
like, oh no, it's terrible.

00:01:26.367 --> 00:01:27.780
And then when he said that,

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:30.233
and I was like, I don't really remember.

00:01:30.233 --> 00:01:31.066
(all laughing)

00:01:31.066 --> 00:01:33.080
- You blacked out. That's
so exciting though.

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:34.894
Congratulations, that's so exciting!

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:36.718
(audience cheers)

00:01:36.718 --> 00:01:38.836
I love that it was on film!

00:01:38.836 --> 00:01:39.993
That's so cool.

